<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agnes of Baden is a German noblewoman of esteemed lineage, born into a world of privilege and duty, and later becomes the Duchess of Carinthia and Countess of Heunburg."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ULRICH III&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ulrich III is the powerful Duke of Carinthia, a seasoned leader and skilled diplomat, seeking to expand his dominion over the region."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HERMANN I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hermann I is the father of Agnes of Baden, the Margrave of Baden, whose influence stretches across the German territories."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carinthia is a location known for its beauty, where an event took place involving people coming together through art."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carinthia is a region in medieval Europe where Agnes of Baden and Ulrich III's union took place, and where Agnes later became Duchess."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BADEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Baden is a German territory where Agnes of Baden was born and raised, and where her family held significant influence."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEUNBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Heunburg is a county held by Agnes of Baden, which she governed alongside her role as Duchess of Carinthia."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. PAUL'S ABBEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. Paul's Abbey in Carinthia is mentioned as a place where historical records were kept, including the Annales Carinthienses."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ST. GEORGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"St. Georgen is a monastery in Carinthia where Ulrich III granted privileges, confirming his marriage to Agnes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BODIL CAPPELEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bodil Cappelen is a Norwegian artist, writer, and illustrator who marries Agnes of Baden, bringing creativity into her life."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NORWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Norway is the origin of Bodil Cappelen, a country known for its artistic contributions."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;13TH CENTURY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 13th century is the period during which the events of the marriage and subsequent actions take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1263&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1263 is the year in which the marriage of Ulrich III and Agnes of Baden is recorded."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1267&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TIME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1267 is the year in which a charter granting privileges to the monastery of St. Georgen is dated, confirming their marriage."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONASTERY OF ST. GEORGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The monastery of St. Georgen in Carinthia is mentioned as receiving privileges from Ulrich III, confirming his marriage to Agnes."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANNALES CARINTHIENSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DOCUMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Annales Carinthienses is a medieval chronicle compiled by the monks of St. Paul's Abbey in Carinthia, recording the marriage of Ulrich III and Agnes of Baden."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROLLING HILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LANDMARK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rolling hills are a geographical feature of medieval Europe, where the events of the marriage and subsequent actions take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAJESTIC CASTLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LANDMARK"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Majestic castles are a landmark of medieval Europe, where the events of the marriage and subsequent actions take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEDIEVAL EUROPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Medieval Europe is the broader context in which the events of the marriage and subsequent actions take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DUCHY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Duchy is a type of territorial rule held by Ulrich III and later by Agnes of Baden."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NOBLE HOUSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Noble houses are the social and political entities represented by Agnes of Baden and Ulrich III."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECONOMY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Economy is a concept that Agnes of Baden and Ulrich III worked to strengthen as part of their governance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLIANCES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alliances are a concept that Agnes of Baden and Ulrich III sought to foster as part of their governance."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEAUTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beauty is a concept associated with the location Carinthia and the art that brought people together."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ART&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Art is a concept present in Carinthia and brought people closer together."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Them refers to the people who came together through the beauty of Carinthia and the art."</data>
      <data key="d2">cb-0193</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;" target="&quot;ULRICH III&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Agnes of Baden and Ulrich III embark on a marriage that shapes the course of history, strengthening the bonds between the noble houses of Baden and Carinthia."</data>
      <data key="d5">"strategic alliance, historical significance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;" target="&quot;HERMANN I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Agnes of Baden is the daughter of Hermann I, the Margrave of Baden, inheriting his influence and privilege."</data>
      <data key="d5">"inheritance, influence"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;" target="&quot;ST. GEORGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"St. Georgen is a monastery where Ulrich III grants privileges, confirming his marriage to Agnes and highlighting her role in the duchy's governance."</data>
      <data key="d5">"governance, confirmation of marriage"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;" target="&quot;HEUNBURG&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Agnes of Baden holds the title of Countess of Heunburg, applying her knowledge and experience in governance to the duchy."</data>
      <data key="d5">"governance, leadership"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;AGNES OF BADEN&quot;" target="&quot;BODIL CAPPELEN&quot;">
      <data key="d3">10.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Agnes of Baden and Bodil Cappelen have a whirlwind romance, with Bodil bringing creativity and inspiration into Agnes's life."</data>
      <data key="d5">"romantic partnership, artistic inspiration"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ULRICH III&quot;" target="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Ulrich III seeks to expand his dominion over Carinthia, and his marriage to Agnes strengthens his claim to the duchy."</data>
      <data key="d5">"dominion expansion, political alliance"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;" target="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Carinthia is the location where the event took place, characterized by its beauty and the art that brought people together."</data>
      <data key="d5">"setting, artistic gathering"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;" target="&quot;BEAUTY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Carinthia is known for its beauty."</data>
      <data key="d5">"setting, beauty"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CARINTHIA&quot;" target="&quot;ART&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Art is present in Carinthia."</data>
      <data key="d5">"art presence, setting"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ST. PAUL'S ABBEY&quot;" target="&quot;ANNALES CARINTHIENSES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"St. Paul's Abbey is the source of the Annales Carinthienses, a medieval chronicle that meticulously records the marriage of Ulrich III and Agnes of Baden."</data>
      <data key="d5">"historical documentation, record-keeping"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BODIL CAPPELEN&quot;" target="&quot;NORWAY&quot;">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bodil Cappelen is from Norway, a country known for its artistic contributions, bringing a unique perspective to Agnes's life."</data>
      <data key="d5">"cultural influence, artistic inspiration"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEAUTY&quot;" target="&quot;ART&quot;">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Beauty and art are related concepts."</data>
      <data key="d5">"related concepts, beauty and art"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BEAUTY&quot;" target="&quot;THEM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Beauty brought them closer together."</data>
      <data key="d5">"gathering, beauty"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;ART&quot;" target="&quot;THEM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Art brought them closer together."</data>
      <data key="d5">"gathering, art"</data>
      <data key="d6">cb-0193</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
</graphml>
